relay	UNKNOWN STEP	   of this handoff.
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	2. Read .claude/agent-memory/test-engineer/MEMORY.md
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	   for anything relevant you've learned on past issues.
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	3. If this task touches one of the standard docs
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	   (docs/PROJECT_DEFINITION.md, docs/RTVM.md, docs/SDD.md,
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	   docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md), check whether it already
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	   exists before writing to it — every project starts with
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	   a pre-structured skeleton for these. Fill in that
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	   existing structure; don't replace it with something new.
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	4. Do the work the issue is asking of you.
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	5. Post one comment on the issue before you finish — no
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	   matter what happened. This isn't conditional on
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	   success: if you completed the task, say what you did;
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	   if you hit an error, ran out of information you
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	   couldn't resolve, or got blocked by something outside
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	   your control, say that instead, as specifically as you
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	   can. The comment thread should never go quiet with no
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	   record of what was attempted. Prefix it with your role
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	   name (e.g. "Software Engineer:").
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	6. Hand off by running exactly one command:
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	     gh issue edit 5 \
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	       --remove-label "agent:test-engineer" \
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	       --remove-label "status:in-progress" \
relay	UNKNOWN STEP	       --add-label "agent:<next-role>"
